Mojotron: the keys
==================

You move with one group of keys and fire with another; firing is
automatic, in the direction you aim. The groups are set in the game's
options (the menu), and these are the first ones:

  W A S D             move
  Cursor keys         aim and fire
  Space               use the powerup you carry (the diamonds)
  P or Esc            pause (the in-game menu)

Sound and music start off: turn them on in the options, or start with
--enable-sound --enable-music.

A joystick or pad works too: SDL 2 game controllers, one stick to move
and one to aim.

Three of a kind, three of one colour, or three in rainbow order of the
fruit give powerups and extra lives. Finish a level inside its time to
skip three levels and win a life.

From a Shell:
  Mojotron [--fullscreen] [--enable-sound] [--enable-music] [-f res.xml]
  (-f res.xml plays with the original 2002 pictures)

The keys every AmiCradle game has on Right Amiga (GFOpenUp's SDL2.module):
Right Amiga + F window or full screen, + P pause, + Q quit, + M free the
mouse pointer, + S a screenshot in the drawer's Screenshots, and Help
shows this file.
